# Become Lawful Neutral by the ordinary "Issue Request" command, as a Neutral
# character who has stated a Lawful desired alignment. This is the game-play
# half of bd inc-r6ae; tools/check_align_coercion_play.sh reads it.
#
# WHAT IS BEING OBSERVED. Character::AlignedAct (src/Prayer.cpp) moves the
# law/chaos score (alignLC) when a Neutral character commits a Lawful or
# Chaotic act, and must set AL_LAWFUL / AL_CHAOTIC once that score passes its
# threshold -- exactly as its good/evil twin sets AL_GOOD / AL_EVIL. Before the
# fix the else branches that set the two flags were missing, so the score could
# move all the way to the cap and the character's alignment never changed and
# the game never printed "You are now ...". This run prints it.
#
# THE CHARACTER is tools/keys/chargen.keys' standard male orc barbarian,
# Neutral, patron Khasrach. He carries no Diplomacy at all and Intimidate +6
# (0 ranks, +3 Strength, +3 training) -- the sheet says so -- so
# Creature::Request (src/Social.cpp) offers the "Use Intimidate?" prompt and
# the coercion aligned act (AL_NONCHAOTIC|AL_LAWFUL, magnitude 3) fires. That
# is the whole reason an orc barbarian is the right character here: no Bluff,
# no ranks spent, and the Intimidate route is reachable immediately.
#
# THE DESIRED ALIGNMENT is stated with the character sheet's '[D] Alignment'
# command (src/Managers.cpp), an ordinary player command, and set to Lawful
# Neutral. Without it AlignedAct clamps the score back to zero as a designed
# guard, and no number of coercions could ever show the fix.
#
# THE VICTIM is a human conjured by wizard mode, one square east. Wizard mode
# sets up state a player could reach -- a talkable, non-evil creature to issue
# a request to -- but every coercion below is the ordinary command. The victim
# cannot answer: Freeze Monsters is on, and a human has no fear resistance, so
# the Intimidate path takes the early-out at src/Social.cpp:1283. The aligned
# act sits ABOVE that early-out, so the act fires and the check still bounds
# the run.
#
# WHY "Go To Location" AND ESC. The aligned act fires before the request is
# chosen and before any skill check, so each coercion aborts at the location
# prompt. An aborted request sets no TRIED flag, so the same victim can be
# coerced again and again -- one summon, no consumables, no waiting for a new
# day. A chosen request that then failed would mark the victim TRIED and stop
# the run after one attempt.
#
# THE COUNT. alignLC starts at 0 and each coercion costs 3, so the threshold at
# |20| is crossed on the seventh (alignLC = -21). Eight are sent for margin;
# the eighth changes nothing and prints nothing, which is itself correct.
#
# Determinism: seed 1, tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat. Every menu is
# reached by name through @choose, and each dump names its own screen.

@include chargen.keys

.*2
@dump:arrival

d               # character sheet
@until "Desired Alignment" D
@choose "Lawful Neutral"
@dump:desired
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
@expect "Freeze Monsters"
DOWN*10
@expect "all monsters are denied their"
SPACE
@expect "Wizard Mode Options"
ESC
@dump:frozen

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Humans"
@choose "human"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:summoned

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce1
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce2
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce3
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce4
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce5
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce6
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce7
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

y
@choose "Issue Request"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "Use Intimidate?" y
@dump:coerce8
@choose "Go To Location"
ESC

v
@dump:messages
ESC

d
@dump:sheet-after
ESC
@quit
